        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "38d30287-f8b2-5d6f-a299-4a55da0df439",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-Claude Trichet, Mario Draghi, Silvio Berlusconi\n- Organizations: European Central Bank, Financial Stability Board, Bank of Italy, Italian government\n- Events: 5 August 2011 ECB letter to Italy, European banking crisis\n- Roles: ECB President, FSB Chairman, Governor of the Bank of Italy\n\nFacts:\n- From 2005 to 2011, Mario Draghi served as Governor of the Bank of Italy.\n- From 2009 to 2011, Mario Draghi served as Chairman of the Financial Stability Board.\n- On 5 August 2011, during the European banking crisis, Jean-Claude Trichet and Mario Draghi sent a secret letter to the Italian government led by Silvio Berlusconi.\n- On 5 August 2011, Jean-Claude Trichet and Mario Draghi urged the Italian government to implement a series of economic measures as soon as possible.\n- Since November 2011, Mario Draghi has served as President of the European Central Bank.\n- Mario Draghi was born on 3 September 1947 and is an Italian economist.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8e7ee2f6-950b-52ef-8fa5-4fae156a1f28",
        "text": "Page: Letter of ECB to Italy on 5th August 2011. Sentence: On 5th August 2011, during dramatic crisis of European banks, the former governor of ECB, Jean Claude Trichet, together with Mario Draghi, wrote a \"secret\" letter to Italian government, at the time led by Silvio Berlusconi, in which they pushed for a series of economic measures \"to be implemented as soon as possible\".\nPage: Mario Draghi. Sentence: Mario Draghi {'1': \", '2': \", '3': 'OMRI', '4': \"} (] ; born 3 September 1947) is an Italian economist who has served as President of the European Central Bank since November 2011.\nPage: Mario Draghi. Sentence: He previously served as Chairman of the Financial Stability Board from 2009 to 2011 and Governor of the Bank of Italy from 2005 to 2011.",
